From: LibreELEC
Subject: [PATCH] meson: drop distutils from the mako check

distutils is gone since Python 3.12; any mako that imports is new enough.
---
diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index 63d487a..6865408 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -1038,9 +1038,7 @@ prog_python = import('python').find_installation('python3')
 has_mako = run_command(
   prog_python, '-c',
   '''
-from distutils.version import StrictVersion
 import mako
-assert StrictVersion(mako.__version__) > StrictVersion("0.8.0")
   ''', check: false)
 if has_mako.returncode() != 0
   error('Python (3.x) mako module >= 0.8.0 required to build mesa.')
